CSV export is in place, and `npm test` passes all 13 tests, including the 6 new ones.

- **`src/csv.ts`**: `entriesToCsv(entries)` writes the `category,cents` header, then one line per entry, joined with `\n` and no trailing newline. A category containing `,`, `"`, `\n` or `\r` is wrapped in double quotes, with any inner `"` doubled. I also quote on `\r`, as the Architect's notes said to.
- **`src/report.ts`**: I added the `entriesToCsv` import first, then `reportCsv(entries)`. It sorts a copy of the entries by category, then by cents, so the input isn't mutated. It uses `<` and `>` rather than `localeCompare`.
- **`test/csv.test.ts`**: the tests cover these cases:
  - an empty list gives just the header;
  - several entries give no trailing newline;
  - a comma in a category gets quoted;

